Here's a JavaScript function that accepts text and posts messages via the Slack API to a specified channel:

```javascript
function postToSlack(text, channel) {
  const webhookUrl = 'https://hooks.slack.com/services/XXXXX/XXXXX/XXXXXX'; // Replace with your webhook URL
  const payload = {
    channel: channel,
    text: text
  };

  fetch(webhookUrl, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      'Content-Type': 'application/json'
    },
    body: JSON.stringify(payload)
  })
    .then(response => response.json())
    .catch(error => console.error('Error posting to Slack:', error));
}

// Example usage
postToSlack('Hello, world!', '#general');
```

Make sure to replace `XXXXX`, `XXXXX`, and `XXXXXX` with your actual Slack webhook URL and channel name.

