To get your relational data from your Microsoft SQL database into a Neo4j graph database to view the graph representation of group memberships, you can follow these steps:

1. Install Neo4j Desktop or use the Neo4j Browser to connect to your Neo4j instance.
2. Create a Cypher query to import the data from your Microsoft SQL database. You can use the `neo4j-sql` library to simplify this process. First, install the library using npm or yarn:
```bash
npm install neo4j-sql
```
or
```bash
yarn add neo4j-sql
```
Then, create a Cypher query using the library like this:
```javascript
const { sql } = require('neo4j-sql');

const query = sql`
  WITH [
    acct AS (
      SELECT accountID, AccountGUID FROM Account
    ),
    grp AS (
      SELECT GroupID, GroupGUID FROM Group
    ),
    mbr AS (
      SELECT GroupID, MemberGroupID FROM GroupMemberGroup
    )
  ]

  MERGE (a:Account { id: acct.accountID, guild: acct.AccountGUID })
  ON CREATE SET a.name = acct.accountID;

  MERGE (g:Group { id: grp.GroupID, guild: grp.GroupGUID })
  ON CREATE SET g.name = grp.GroupGUID;

  MERGE (m:MemberGroup { id: mbr.GroupID, guild: mbr.MemberGroupID })
  ON CREATE SET m.name = mbr.MemberGroupID;

  MERGE (a)-[:MEMBER_OF]->(g) WHERE (a.id = m.GroupID AND g.id = m.MemberGroupID);
`;

// Execute the query
const result = await db.query(query);
```
Replace `db` with your Neo4j instance connection. This query will import the data from your Microsoft SQL database into your Neo4j graph database and create nodes and relationships according to the specified schema.

