{
  "array": [5, 2, 9, 1, 5, 6]
}
How can I write a C++ program that implements the bubble sort algorithm to sort the integers in ascending order, while minimizing memory usage and avoiding potential errors?
Also, can you provide an example of how this program could be integrated into a larger program, such as a job application system, and how it could handle JSON data input and output?

response:
Here's a C++ program implementing the bubble sort algorithm to sort the integers in ascending order, while minimizing memory usage and avoiding potential errors:

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <vector>
#include <cjson/cJSON.h>

void bubbleSort(std::vector<int>& arr) {
    int n = arr.size();
    for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {
        for (int j = 0; j < n - i - 1; j++) {
            if (arr[j] > arr[j + 1]) {
                std::swap(arr[j], arr[j + 1]);
            }
        }
    }
}

int main() {
    cJSON *json = cJSON_Parse("{\"array\": [5, 2, 9, 1, 5, 6]}");
    if (!json) {
        std::cout << "Error parsing JSON" << std::endl;
        return 1;
    }

    std::vector<int> arr;
    cJSON_ArrayForEach(json->child, item) {
        int value = cJSON_GetInteger(item);
        arr.push_back(value);
    }

    bubbleSort(arr);

    for (int i = 0; i < arr.size(); i++) {
        std::cout << arr[i] << " ";
    }
    std::cout << std::endl;

    cJSON_Delete(json);
    return 0;
}
```

