2. Implement a scroll event listener that checks if the user is trying to scroll to an uncofused section. If so, prevent the scroll and animate a force against it.
3. When the user completes a task in the focused section, update the state management to scroll to the next section and make the previously unfocused section focused.
4. Allow the user to scroll up to see their past tasks, but prevent them from scrolling past the last focused section by adding a bounce effect in the scroll animation.

