To create a socket for chat rooms, you'll need to use PHP's built-in sockets extension and the Socket.IO library. Here's an example of how to set up a socket server using these libraries:

1. Install the Socket.IO library using Composer by running the following command:
```bash
composer require socketio/socket.io
```
1. Create a new PHP file called `socket_server.php` and add the following code:
```php
<?php

require_once 'vendor/autoload.php';

use SocketIO\SocketIO;

$server = new SocketIO();
$server->on('connection', function ($client) {
    echo "Client connected\n";

    $client->on('disconnect', function () {
        echo "Client disconnected\n";
    });

    $client->on('message', function ($message) {
        echo "Received message: {$message}\n";

        // Broadcast the message to all connected clients
        $server->broadcast($message);
